      },
      "message": "feat(tools): a tapered mill has a tip form (sharp, flat, ball)\n\n`Tool` gets `tip_form` (sharp, flat or ball; default sharp) and\n`tip_diameter`. The tip math of #895 is in the new\n`crates/tools/src/taper.rs`: the sanity rules, the drawn profile and the\nmeridian. A sharp taper keeps its profile, meridian and stamp.\n\n- The project file, the tool library file, the catalog reader and MCP\n  (`edit_tool`, `add_tool`, `set_tool_cutter_params`) carry the fields.\n- The catalog adds a flat-tip chamfer mill, a tapered flat end mill and\n  a tapered ball nose.\n- Every operation refuses a flat or ball tip by name, at creation and at\n  generation and the post, until a generator reads it.\n- A `.camproj` with a flat or ball tip says version 79 and a `.camtools`\n  says version 6, so an older build refuses the file. A file without one\n  keeps its old number. The project step is isolated in\n  `project/file.rs` (see docs/decisions/3368-taper-tip-form.md).\n- The tool editor shows a Tip form row and a Tip diameter row.\n\nFixes #3368\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
